# Uniqueness of epic `∗`-regular envelopes ([JZLA20, Theorem 2.9])

[JZLA20, Theorem 2.9] (quoting [Ja17base, Theorem 6.3]): two **epic `∗`-regular `R`-rings** are
isomorphic as soon as they induce the same rank function on matrices over `R`.  Concretely, if
`φ₁ : R →+* U₁`, `φ₂ : R →+* U₂` are epic ring homomorphisms into `∗`-regular rings with faithful
rank functions `rk₁`, `rk₂` and

  `rk₁(φ₁(A)) = rk₂(φ₂(A))`  for every matrix `A` over `R`,

then there is a ring isomorphism `e : U₁ ≃+* U₂` commuting with `φ₁`, `φ₂` and preserving the rank
functions.

This is the tool with which [JZLA20, Theorem 6.1] identifies the two `K[H]`-rings
`U_H` and `R(f_ω(φ(K[N])[t^{±1};τ]), P^U_{ω,τ})` — both are epic `∗`-regular envelopes of the rank
function `rk|_{K[H]}` — thereby transferring the division-ring conclusion of
[JZLA20, Proposition 5.1] from `P^U_{ω,τ}` back to the envelope `U` of the theorem.

The statement is recorded here as the `Prop`-valued definition `EpicEnvelopeUnique`.
-/
import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.ORHughesFree.Epic
import Submission.Work.ORHughesFree.StarRegular
import Submission.Work.ORHughesFree.SylvesterRank

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

namespace Work.ORHughesFree

/-- **[JZLA20, Theorem 2.9]** ([Ja17base, Theorem 6.3]): two epic `∗`-regular `R`-rings inducing
the same rank function on the matrices over `R` are isomorphic, compatibly with the structure maps
and with the rank functions.

`R` is assumed to be a `∗`-ring and `φ₁`, `φ₂` to be `∗`-homomorphisms: this is **essential** (the
proof compares the two rank functions on the `∗`-subring of `U₁ × U₂` generated by
`{(φ₁ r, φ₂ r)}`, which is a `∗`-subring only when `φ₁, φ₂` intertwine the involutions), and
without it the statement is *false* — with `R = ℚ[x]`, `U₁ = U₂ = ℚ(x)` carrying the trivial
involution, and the two inclusions, the element `(0, x)` of the `∗`-regular closure of the diagonal
copy of `R` has `rk₁∘π₁`-rank `0` and `rk₂∘π₂`-rank `1`. -/
def EpicEnvelopeUnique (R : Type u) [Ring R] [StarRing R] : Prop :=
  ∀ (U₁ : Type u) [Ring U₁] [StarRing U₁] [IsStarRegular U₁]
    (U₂ : Type u) [Ring U₂] [StarRing U₂] [IsStarRegular U₂]
    (φ₁ : R →+* U₁) (φ₂ : R →+* U₂) (rk₁ : SylvesterRank U₁) (rk₂ : SylvesterRank U₂),
    (∀ x : R, φ₁ (star x) = star (φ₁ x)) → (∀ x : R, φ₂ (star x) = star (φ₂ x)) →
    IsEpic φ₁ → IsEpic φ₂ → rk₁.IsFaithful → rk₂.IsFaithful →
    (∀ (n m : ℕ) (A : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin m) R),
      rk₁.rk n m (A.map φ₁) = rk₂.rk n m (A.map φ₂)) →
    ∃ e : U₁ ≃+* U₂, (∀ x : R, e (φ₁ x) = φ₂ x) ∧
      (∀ x : U₁, rk₂.rk 1 1 (oneByOne (e x)) = rk₁.rk 1 1 (oneByOne x))

end Work.ORHughesFree
